This license covers the code I wrote for NonUI. I am chrissyx. The repository is https://github.com/Chrissshere/qemu-nonui

You can use this code, change it, and ship a tool or program made from it. If you do, the rules below apply to that tool, to the changes, and to the program you give people. "Made from it" means your tool includes this code, changes this code, or is built from this code.

The source stays open, and the program stays open. You release the program as open source. You also release the source for that same version, including your changes. A closed program, or a program people cannot rebuild from the source you released, does not follow this license.

You keep at least one reference to me in what you release. The reference is the name chrissyx, or a link to https://github.com/Chrissshere/qemu-nonui, or a link to https://github.com/Chrissshere. One of those is enough. It has to be in the source or in the program where a person can see it.

I have the rights to the code you add and to the changes you make. I can take that code, treat it as my own, change it, ship it, and use it in my own projects. I can do that without asking you, without paying you, and without leaving it under this license. You do not get to revoke that.

Code I did not write stays under its own license. QEMU, Light Touch, and the other pieces the build downloads are not covered by this file. Their notices are in THIRD-PARTY.md. This license does not replace those.

This is provided as is. I am not responsible for what you do with the program, or for the firmware you obtained.
